{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors source code files for changes and provides intelligent suggestions for code improvements, including identifying code smells, recommending design patterns, and highlighting best practices to enhance readability, maintainability, and performance.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.jsx",
      "**/*.tsx",
      "**/*.mjs",
      "**/*.cjs",
      "**/*.py",
      "**/*.java",
      "**/*.cpp",
      "**/*.c",
      "**/*.cs",
      "**/*.go",
      "**/*.rs",
      "**/*.rb",
      "**/*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code in the changed files for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells such as duplicated code, long methods, large classes, excessive parameters, or inappropriate intimacy between classes.\n\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest applicable design patterns that could improve the code structure and maintainability.\n\n3. **Best Practices**: Evaluate adherence to language-specific best practices, naming conventions, and coding standards.\n\n4. **Readability**: Assess code clarity, comment quality, and suggest improvements for better understanding.\n\n5. **Maintainability**: Identify areas that could be refactored for easier future modifications and reduced technical debt.\n\n6. **Performance**: Highlight potential performance bottlenecks or inefficiencies, and suggest optimizations where appropriate.\n\n7. **Security**: Flag any obvious security concerns or vulnerabilities.\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions while maintaining the existing functionality. Prioritize improvements that offer the most value. Be constructive and explain the reasoning behind each suggestion."
  }
}